  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "N.Thirumurthi vs The Commissioner on 11 September, 2024 Author: N.Anand Venkatesh Bench: N.Anand Venkatesh Writ Petition No In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated: 11.09.2024 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice N.Anand Venkatesh Writ Petition No.26460 of 2024 and W.M.P.Nos.28924 & 28925 of 2024 N.Thirumurthi ... Petitioner Vs. 1.The Commissioner, Food Safety and Drug Administration Department, Anna Salai, DMS Compound, Chennai - 600 006. 2.The Designated Officer, Food Safety and Drug Administration Department, Salem District, Salem - 636 001. 3.The Director of Municipal Administration, No.75, Santhome High Road, MRC Nagar, R.A.Puram, Chennai - 600 028. 4.The Commissioner, Namakkal City Municipal Corporation, Namakkal - 637 001. ... Respondents Writ Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitut India seeking issuance of a Writ of Certiorarified Mandamus calling the records relating to the impugned charge memorandum issued by th https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 1/6 Writ Petition second respondent in Na.Ka.No.458/A1/FSSA/2018 dated 19.03.2018 N.Thirumurthi vs The Commissioner on 11 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/18179656/ 1 and quash the same and consequently, to direct the respondents 1 an to expunge the statement recorded by the second respondent in the Service Register of the petitioner to the fact that the disciplinar proceedings is still pending for issuing final orders within a reas period as may be fixed by this Court. For Petitioner : Mr.T.Ranganathan For Respondents : Mr.M.Bindran, Additional Government Pleader [R1 & R2] Dr.T.Seenivasan, Special Government Pleader [R3 & R ***** ORDER",
    "facts": "The case of the petitioner is that he was working as a Food Safety Officer and a charge memo under Rule 17(b) of the Tamil Nadu Civil Services (Discipline and Appeal) Rules, 1955, came to be issued by the second respondent. The first respondent called for enquiry on 21.05.2018 and the petitioner appeared before the first respondent. Accordingly, the petitioner was relieved from the first respondent department on 31.05.2018. The petitioner was under the impression that the entire disciplinary proceedings has come to an end. Since the same was not considered, the present writ petition has been filed challenging the impugned remarks made by the second respondent in the service register of the petitioner.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
